# AXIS Current Execution Architecture

The current implemented execution pipeline is:

User
↓
Agent
↓
Intent Engine
↓
Planner
↓
Executor
↓
Runtime
↓
Plugin Manager
↓
Plugin
↓
Result / Response

Memory is accessed through Runtime.

Command Engine is implemented and tested as a supporting plan-to-task conversion subsystem. It is not currently a required stage in `Agent.process()`.

Do not reorder, bypass, or duplicate the current execution boundaries without an approved architecture decision.

# Architecture Evolution

AXIS has two architectural dimensions:

1. Current implementation architecture
   - Describes what exists and is tested today.
   - Must remain synchronized with the implementation.

2. Future vision and planned capabilities
   - Describes systems AXIS may implement later.
   - Must never be represented as currently implemented.

Do not implement future architecture prematurely.

Prefer incremental, tested evolution of the existing system.